# Skill Module Template
#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="template"
PURPOSE="Meta-skeleton for authoring new .chloeai skill modules"

# ============================================================
# HOW TO USE THIS TEMPLATE
# ============================================================
#
# 1. Copy this file to ai_modules/<skill_name>.chloeai (project scope)
#    or to ~/Documents/Projects/GitHub/.claude/skills/<skill_name>/SKILL.md
#    (global scope, markdown form).
# 2. Fill in the frontmatter (TYPE, MODULE, VERSION, LINEAGE, SCOPE).
# 3. Replace each section's body with the actual protocol.
# 4. Add a row to ai_context/START_HERE.md File Map under
#    "Operating charter".
# 5. If the skill replaces or supersedes prior conventions, update
#    those references in CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md.
#
# A skill module is DIFFERENT from a personality module:
#   - Personality (hi_mode.chloeai): values, voice, rules. Always-on.
#   - Skill (this template): a triggered protocol with phases and
#     stop conditions. Activates on a defined trigger.
#
# Naming convention:
#   - Module name uses snake_case: project_brainstorming
#   - File name matches the skill: brainstorming.chloeai

# ============================================================
# FRONTMATTER (replace with real values when copying)
# ============================================================
#
# TYPE="skill"
# MODULE="project_<skill_name>"
# VERSION="Charter-<SkillName>-Project-YYYY-MM"
# LINEAGE="(adapted from <source> if applicable, else 'original')"
# SCOPE="single project"

# ============================================================
# PURPOSE
# ============================================================
#
# One paragraph: what does this skill enable, and why does it exist?
# State the problem the skill is solving in one sentence, then the
# approach it takes in one or two more.

# ============================================================
# WHEN TO INVOKE
# ============================================================
#
# Concrete triggers. Examples:
# - When the owner says "let's plan a feature"
# - When ai_context/project_brief.md still has placeholder comments
# - When a bug has resisted 2+ attempted fixes
#
# A skill should have AT LEAST ONE objective trigger (file state,
# error count, etc.) and may also have subjective triggers
# (owner intent).

# ============================================================
# PROTOCOL
# ============================================================
#
# Numbered phases or steps. Each phase should have:
# - A clear entry condition (when does this phase start?)
# - A defined output (what does the phase produce?)
# - An exit condition (what allows the next phase to begin?)
#
# Phase 1: <NAME>
#   Entry: <when this phase starts>
#   Do: <ordered actions>
#   Output: <artifact, decision, or signal>
#   Exit: <condition to advance>
#
# Phase 2: ...

# ============================================================
# RULES
# ============================================================
#
# Must / must-not statements. Examples:
# - MUST present design before writing code
# - MUST NOT propose multiple fixes in parallel
# - MUST log every assumption explicitly
#
# Keep this list short (3-7 items). If it grows beyond 7, split
# into protocol phases.

# ============================================================
# STOP CONDITIONS
# ============================================================
#
# When does this skill PAUSE and return control to the owner?
# Examples:
# - Owner cannot answer 2+ core questions
# - Source state contradicts a stated assumption
# - 3+ attempted fixes have failed
#
# Stop is mandatory. Silence is not consent.

# ============================================================
# WRITEBACK TARGETS
# ============================================================
#
# When the skill produces durable output (decisions, designs, audits),
# where does the output land?
# Examples:
# - Designs -> docs/<topic>-design.md + ai_context/decision_log.md entry
# - Bug findings -> AI_HANDOFF.chloeai entry
# - Scope captures -> ai_context/project_brief.md + CURRENT_MISSION.md

# ============================================================
# SELF-TEST
# ============================================================
#
# - Test: Echo module name        --> Expect: "<module name>"
# - Test: Name a stop condition   --> Expect: <one of the stop conditions>
# - Test: Name the first phase    --> Expect: <Phase 1 name>

# ============================================================
# CHANGELOG
# ============================================================
#
# <VERSION_TAG> (YYYY-MM-DD, <author>):
#   <one-line summary of what changed>

# END OF SKILL TEMPLATE
